<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $162.6 mln Nov 18.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $162.6 mln Nov 18.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $162.6 million surplus on November 18 according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON NOVEMBER 18</p>
<p>Exports: $182.2 million</p>
<p>Imports: $146.8 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $367.2 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $240 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $162.6 million</p>
<p>NOVEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.891 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.871 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $4.410 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.751 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.679 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5418</p>
</text>
